        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Create Claw agent and root install record",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nImplements the second RFC 0016 slice, stacked on #101328:\n\n- `openclaw claws add <source> --yes` requires explicit consent and creates exactly one new agent plus one new workspace.\n- Appends a portable `agents.list[]` entry while preserving `agents.defaults`, existing agents, bindings, models, providers, auth, and unrelated config.\n- Rechecks agent-id and configured-workspace collisions inside the concurrent config transform.\n- Atomically reserves the workspace before config mutation and removes the empty reservation if config commit fails.\n- Persists one root `openclaw.clawInstallRecord.v1` in shared SQLite state with package/development identity, integrity, final agent id, workspace, generated-config digest, status, and timestamps.\n- Returns versioned `openclaw.clawAddResult.v1` JSON with `stability: \"experimental\"` and distinguishes complete, partial, and failed adds.\n- Keeps all Claws commands behind `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`.\n\nThis slice intentionally accepts mutation only for manifests containing portable agent settings and an empty workspace. Declared workspace files, skills, plugins, MCP servers, or cron jobs fail with `unsupported_components` before mutation; later stacked PRs add those resource owners in RFC order. No declared component is silently skipped.\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\n- Depends on: #101328 grouped schema and read-only add plan\n- This PR: agent/workspace creation and root install ownership\n- Next: confined bootstrap/supporting workspace files and managed hashes\n\n## Validation\n\nBranch head: `f2f90aa72694a20428d10c7329106e512273ef84`\n\n```text\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n  src/claws/schema.test.ts src/claws/feed.test.ts src/claws/experimental.test.ts \\\n  src/claws/provenance.test.ts src/cli/claws-cli.test.ts \\\n  src/cli/program/command-registry.test.ts \\\n  src/cli/program/root-command-descriptions.test.ts src/cli/argv.test.ts \\\n  src/claws/lifecycle.e2e.test.ts\n# 195 tests passed across 4 Vitest shards\n\npnpm exec oxlint src/claws src/cli/claws-cli.ts \\\n  src/cli/claws-cli.runtime.ts src/cli/claws-cli.test.ts \\\n  src/cli/program/core-command-descriptors.ts\n# 0 warnings, 0 errors\n\ngit diff --check\nnode scripts/check-no-conflict-markers.mjs\n# passed\n```\n\nFull `pnpm exec tsgo --noEmit --pretty false` reaches only the pre-existing unrelated `src/secrets/config-io.ts` TS4058.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nWith isolated `HOME`, `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR`, and `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH`, this command completed:\n\n```text\nOPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1 \\\nOPENCLAW_DISABLE_BUNDLED_PLUGINS=1 \\\nnode --import tsx src/entry.ts claws add \\\n  src/claws/fixtures/minimal-agent.claw.json --yes --json\n```\n\nObserved result:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"openclaw.clawAddResult.v1\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"agentId\": \"internal-triage\",\n  \"record\": \"openclaw.clawInstallRecord.v1\"\n}\n```\n\nThe resulting config contained one `internal-triage` agent with only the manifest's portable settings and derived workspace. SQLite contained one `claw_installs` row for that agent, local development identity/version, workspace, and `complete` status.\n",
        "branch": "user/giodl/claws-pr3-feed-plan",
